<title>LEBANON: Banque Audi reports strong 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Banque Audi reports strong 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated net profits of Lebanon's Banque Audi and its Audi Investment Bank (Infibank) subsidiary rose 52.5 percent in 1996, according to audited annual financial results released by the bank on Monday.</p>
<p>The increase in net profits compared with a 57.7 percent rise in 1995.</p>
<p>Banque Audi ranked third among Lebanon's 82 banks in total assets in 1995. It began trading 30 percent of its shares on the Beirut Stock Exchange on January 20 and they have since become the most active shares on the market.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following results (in billions of Lebanese pounds unless otherwise stated. Change on previous year in brackets):</p>
<p>			     1996			 1995</p>
<p>    Net profits	  30.71 (52.5%)	    20.14  (57.7%)</p>
<p>    Assets	    2,862.73 (35.3%)	 2,115.96  (30.3%)</p>
<p>    Deposits	  2,390.82 (27.9%)	 1,869.20  (24.2%)</p>
<p>    Loans		 814.04 (32.2%)	   615.94  (42.9%)</p>
<p>    Equity		172.95 (26.0%)	   137.24 (190.5%)</p>
<p>Other details:</p>
<p>    EPS		    $1.43			$0.96</p>
<p>    NAVS		   $8.04			$6.51</p>
<p>Shares o/s</p>
<p>    (millions)		13,860		     13,200</p>
<p>Net return on</p>
<p>    average assets (%)  1.23			 1.08</p>
<p>    Spread (%)	    3.50			 3.02</p>
<p>    Cost to income (%) 63.55			66.33</p>
<p>Loan loss provision</p>
<p>    to total loans (%)  3.20			 2.41</p>
<p>Return on average</p>
<p>    equity		 19.80			27.79</p>
<p>(Note: the figures for return on average equity were affected by the sharp increase in equity related to the GDR issue in November 1995)</p>
<p>$1 = 1,552 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/1996</p>
<p>$1 = 1,596 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/1995</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (961 1)602057 345723 345740</p>
</text>
